      "text": "Finally, the paper situates its findings within contemporary philological and codicological scholarship—most notably the works of NEUWIRTH, PUIN, SADEGHI, and FEDELI—which have questioned the conventional chronology of the Qurʾān’s written codification. While fully acknowledging the deep reverence Muslims hold for the Qurʾān and its Messenger, this article seeks to recover—from the Qurʾān itself, as God’s infallible word and “a clarification and detailed explanation of everything” (Q 16:89; cf. Q 6:114–115; Q 7:52; Q 12:111; Q 17:9)—its own linguistic testimony, thereby clarifying how certain theological interpretations evolved over time.",
