      "text": "Another verse that supports the viewpoint that Muhammad was never exposed to any prior scripture is Q 29:48\n\nوَمَا كُنتَ تَتْلُوا۟ مِن قَبْلِهِۦ مِن كِتَـٰبٍ وَلَا تَخُطُّهُۥ بِيَمِينِكَ إِذًا لَّٱرْتَابَ ٱلْمُبْطِلُونَ\n\nWa-mā kunta tatlū min qablihi min kitābin wa-lā takhuṭṭuhu bi-yamīnika idhan la-irtāba al-mubṭilūn.\n\n“And you did not recite before it any scripture, nor did you write it with your right hand, otherwise the falsifiers would have doubted.” (Q 29:48)\n\nMuhammad is being accused of deriving the Qurʾān from earlier Abrahamic texts. The use of qablihi (“before it”) is key, for it temporally binds the argument by indicating not illiteracy but prior non-exposure. The Qurʾān rejects the accusation with this verse, stating that he did not engage with earlier scripture either orally or in written form before this revelation, rather than asserting permanent illiteracy.",
