      "text": "Form II (kat-taba كَتَّبَ) → “to make someone write.” Form IV (ʾaktaba أَكْتَبَ) → “to caused to be written / to dictate.”\n\nBecause the verse employs Form VIII, not Form II or IV, the causative reading is grammatically untenable. The morphology itself restricts the meaning to a reflexive act—“he wrote (himself),” not “he caused to be written.”",
