      "text": "The vivid imagery described in Q 68:1 and Q 96:4 indirectly provides further evidence of a writing culture within the community that lacked exposure to any prior revelation.\n\nنٓ وَٱلْقَلَمِ وَمَا يَسْطُرُونَ\n\nNūn. Wa-al-qalami wa-mā yasṭurūn.\n\n“Nūn. By the pen and what they inscribe.” (68:1)\n\nٱلَّذِى عَلَّمَ بِٱلْقَلَمِ\n\nAlladhī ʿallama bi-al-qalam.\n\n“Who taught by the pen.” (96:4)\n\nThese verses suggest literacy within the recipients of the Qurʾān and that writing was intrinsic to revelation from the very beginning.",
